mitting more chips, keeping my options open. If the river improves my hand (Jack, 7, or diamond), I can bet for value. If it doesn't help and opponent bets big, I can fold without losing more. This is the most prudent play given my medium-strength hand and positional disadvantage in reading opponent's strength.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
